# Host rule for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Same syntax on both.
# Copy this file to frontend/public/_redirects before building, so Create React
# App copies it into build/ where the host looks for it.
#
# Order matters. These are evaluated top to bottom and the first match wins, so
# the three 200 rewrites must precede the catch all.
#
# Static files are served before any rule here is consulted, so the 39
# prerendered route shells and every asset resolve normally and never reach the
# catch all.

# No permanent redirects.
#
# There was a 301 here sending the owner's surfer article to the fuller
# replacement, on the reasoning that the replacement supersedes it: same
# category, same tags, every heading covered, plus injury prevention and an FAQ.
# That reasoning still holds and the redirect is still gone.
#
# A 301 removes a page from the site. That article is one of the seven the owner
# actually published and it is live and indexed today, so removing it is his
# call and not a consequence of a rewrite. The cross canonical in
# src/seo/consolidatedSlugs.js does the consolidation work anyway: search engines
# fold the signals into the replacement, and a reader who follows an old link
# still gets the article instead of being bounced.
#
# To make it a redirect after he agrees, one line:
#   /blog/why-surfers-in-santa-cruz-should-lift-weights  /blog/strength-training-for-surfers-santa-cruz  301!

# Client only routes with no prerendered directory. Without these, a staff
# member who refreshes /staff/dashboard is locked out of the CRM and every
# review link is dead.
#
# They point at app-shell.html, not index.html. index.html is the homepage, and
# serving it here handed a cold load of /staff/login the homepage's
# index,follow directive and the homepage's canonical. app-shell.html carries
# noindex,nofollow in the markup.
/staff/*                 /app-shell.html   200
/review/*                /app-shell.html   200
/implementation-preview  /app-shell.html   200
/implementation-preview/*  /app-shell.html   200

# Everything else that did not match a real file is genuinely not found.
# A SPA catch all returning 200 here would get the sitemap rejected by Search
# Console and the site mis-indexed.
/*                       /404.html     404
